 "summaries": [
  {
   "section": "Tires",
   "text": "The front left tire is below recommended tire tread depth and noted uneven wear. All four tires on the vehicle are of the same brand. All remaining wheel rims appear to be in good condition, and all tires match the manufacturer's specifications and size. No tire or wheel issues were found at the time of inspection."
  },
  {
   "section": "Exterior",
   "text": "There are minor misc scratches around the vehicle. Normal for mileage and most too small to see in photos. The paint shows some wear and tear that is consistent with age and mileage."
  },
  {
   "section": "Interior",
   "text": "I observed that the steering wheel shows wear. There is light wear to the seats. Normal for mileage. The inner door panels show wear. The interior trim shows normal wear. I noted that the fabric on the left armrest is chipped. The center console shows wear. The carpet shows normal wear."
  },
  {
   "section": "Mechanical",
   "text": "The engine oil is dirty and should be changed. There was no burning oil smell in the engine compartment after running the vehicle. Fasteners in the engine bay appeared generally intact and in place. Hoses, belts, axle boots, and visible bushings appeared sound."
  },
  {
   "section": "Road Test",
   "text": "A scan of the ECU revealed no current, pending, or historic fault codes. The vehicle accelerated as expected, and it performed well in terms of ride quality, acceleration, and handling. The brakes were firm, with no detectable pulsation."
  }
